Colin wrote:
> Does praying at an altar to generate holy water count against my prayer
> timeout?
>
> Also, how can I acquire more waters, either holy or otherwise?

Any successful prayer counts against your prayer timeout; praying at a
colaligned altar has all the usual effects of prayer, and then just
also happens to give the added bonus effect of blessing any and all
water that's on the floor.

To acquire water, you should start with (almost) any random potion that
you don't need and then dip it in water twice; dipping stacks of less
than 2 into potions of water wastes water instead of creating it, but
you can also use fountains for this (and once you get water walking
boots or an amulet of magical breathing or controllable polymorph, you
can use pools of water for this purpose, which is good because they
don't run out like fountains do).  The other main option is to zap a
wand of cancellation at the random potion.

Hope this helps!

